  --- ADVISOR ----------------------------------------------
  [!] Don't miss Yoel among the dying pilgrims
      Yoel of Londor is the one living pilgrim among the dead ones at the broken bridge just before the Undead Settlement entrance (where you arrive from the banner). If you progress without talking to him you lose his free levels, Yuria of Londor, and the entire Usurpation of Fire ending path. Talk to him before moving on - he then waits at Firelink.
  [!] Do NOT kill Hodrick when he invades
      Holy Knight Hodrick invades near the Pit of Hollows in the Undead Settlement. Do not kill him during the invasion - you need him alive to join the Mound-makers covenant. To join: talk to the giant cage-carrying enemy, climb into his cage, and you'll be carried to Hodrick in the Pit of Hollows.
  [!] Talk to the Giant Archer before farming the graveyard
      A Giant in the tall tower fires huge arrows into the white-birch graveyard. Climb his tower and talk to him FIRST to receive a Token of Friendship - from then on his arrows kill hollows but ignore you, making the graveyard items (including the Mortician's Ashes) safe to grab.
  [>] Siegward at the tower elevator (questline start)
      Siegward of Catarina (Onion Knight) is stuck at the tower elevator near the Giant's tower. Elevator trick: step on the pressure plate, immediately step OFF so the second platform descends, then ride the other one. Join him to fight the Fire Demon below - you get a Siegbrau, and his questline (which later determines whether Greirat survives Irithyll) only advances if he wins this fight with you.
  [i] Missed: Claymore on the dragon bridge
      The Claymore - an excellent quality weapon that scales with both Str and Dex - is still on the High Wall, on the platform where the dragon breathes fire. How to get back: Warp to the Tower on the Wall bonfire, head to the dragon bridge, sprint across to bait the flame downward, then grab the Claymore on the upper platform during the window.
